     "result_text_tail": "d from the pack. It found one wrong title (it called Zipcart's contribution \"profit\" and said \"only city\" instead of \"densest city\") and a few claims stated more strongly than the evidence supports. I fixed all of them.\n- A second, independent source wasn't possible, since you limited me to the pack.\n- The slide software shows most dollar figures on cards and in tables to one decimal (\u2212$2.7 rather than \u2212$2.67), while the charts and the workbook keep cents.\n\n**Choices I made on your behalf:**\n- **Mode:** a deep deck (43 slides, including a 7-page appendix), because this is a board launch decision.\n- **Audience:** the board, deciding to approve or reject.\n- **Theme:** navy.\n- **Problem statement:** the launch question, judged against your two constraints: profitability within current cash and 12 months of runway.\n- **Out of scope:** new funding, other cities, and partnering with Zipcart or QuickBasket.\n- **Cash reading:** I assumed the founders' $9.5M already covers the software business's own burn, which is the reading most favourable to the launch. If it doesn't, the plan needs $16.7M.\n- **Not tested:** the founders' claim that \"nobody owns the Midwest\", because the pack has no data on operators in those cities. It's listed in the appendix.\n\nNext, I can switch to another theme, or turn the flat-cost assumption into a sensitivity analysis once the CFO's budget is in.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `parcelbird-now.pptx`\n- `parcelbird-now-sources.xlsx`\n- `parcelbird-now.json`"
    }
